Knowledge and IP reuse (CON-IP-06)

Issuer: Nivy Advisory s. r. o. · IČO 52 109 338 · Mlynské nivy 16, 821 09 Bratislava

Firm methods, templates and accelerators stay firm property unless the statement of work assigns them.
The client keeps rights in its pre-existing material and, as defined in the contract, in the configured deliverable. Under the Copyright Act (zákon č. 185/2015 Z. z.) economic rights cannot be assigned outright, so the contract grants a licence — its scope, territory, term and exclusivity must be stated explicitly.
Software written for a client by our employees belongs to the firm as an employee work, and is licensed onward to the client on the agreed terms.
Third-party and open-source components are listed with their licences before delivery; a copyleft licence in a client product needs approval.
Anonymised lessons learned may enter the firm knowledge base after the engagement closes, with names, figures and anything else identifying removed.
A client logo or case study is published only with written client consent.

